From d057d68645278b2806d6facf91530ca0c09a64d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 22:20:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] tokenizer: drop per-merge string allocations in the BPE
 session (w7-5 s3)

The per-request pi path census (tools/server path post-W6-6) showed the
merge loop at ~77% of every full/delta tokenization: each merge paid
~13 heap allocations (left/right/concat stale check, rank-lookup pair
copies, bigram text). The bigram now carries sizes only - stale entries
are detected like llm_bigram_spm already does - and the rank lookups
reuse SSO scratch strings. The GPT-2 byte encoding loses its provably
identity decode/re-encode round-trip per word and its per-byte hash
lookup. Output is bit-identical by construction.

Gate: 16/16 real pi prompts (T12 rounds) token sha equal across
pre-change, post-change and the pinned trunk tokenizer in Python;
formatted-text sha unchanged; test-tokenizer-0 15/15 vocabs;
test-token-prefix-cache and test-chat-template-cache all PASS.
Tokenize full 741->412 ms on the 412 KB pi corpus (1.8x), steady
splice ~2.5x; llama-server builds rc=0 (container builder).

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai <glm@z.ai>
